{"project":"platform/upstream/llvm","branch":"tizen_base","id":"I28171720d5bbbf9eaf491cdafc0aee0b43f9cd06","number":361395,"subject":"x86_64: hybrid linkage, BOLT clang, fixed flags and archives","owner":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"url":"https://review.tizen.org/gerrit/c/platform/upstream/llvm/+/361395","hashtags":[],"createdOn":1794500787,"lastUpdated":1794648253,"open":true,"status":"NEW","comments":[{"timestamp":1794500787,"reviewer":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"message":"Uploaded patch set 1."},{"timestamp":1794646345,"reviewer":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"message":"Uploaded patch set 2."},{"timestamp":1794646378,"reviewer":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"message":"Uploaded patch set 3."},{"timestamp":1794648202,"reviewer":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"message":"Patch Set 1:\n\nPatch Set 1 - Part 1: hybrid LLVM linkage on x86_64\n\nHow to review: this change is uploaded as three cumulative patch sets.\nPS1 contains Part 1. Compare PS1 -\u003e PS2 to see Part 2 (BOLT) alone,\nand PS2 -\u003e PS3 to see Part 3 (flags and archive conversion) alone.\n\nWhat Part 1 does:\n- On x86_64, LLVM/Clang tools link against libLLVM and libclang-cpp,\n  while clang, lld and llvm-ar stay statically linked (these are the\n  binaries qemu-accel uses for cross builds).\n- It is selected by TIZEN_HYBRID_LINK, which only the x86_64 recipe\n  sets. Without it, the new CMake helpers return immediately and the\n  upstream behavior is kept.\n- Files: llvm/cmake/modules/AddLLVM.cmake,\n  clang/cmake/modules/AddClang.cmake, lld/cmake/modules/AddLLD.cmake,\n  the clang, lld and llvm-ar CMakeLists.txt, packaging/llvm.spec.\n\narmv7l/aarch64: build behavior is unchanged. AddLLVM.cmake and\nAddClang.cmake are installed on every architecture, so the ARM\nllvm-devel and clang packages carry the new CMake text. Against the\npre-change QB builds (1216401/1216400), 60 of 68 ARM packages are\nidentical and the other 8 differ only in these two files.\n\nRollback: revert Part 1.\n\nValidation: PS1 was not built on its own; it was validated as part of\nthe complete series (see the PS3 note)."},{"timestamp":1794648222,"reviewer":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"message":"Patch Set 2:\n\nPatch Set 2 - adds Part 2: BOLT-optimized clang on x86_64\n\nCompare PS1 -\u003e PS2 to see Part 2 only. Files:\n- packaging/clang-bolt-helper.py (new)\n- packaging/clang-bolt-v2.fdata.xz (new, binary BOLT profile,\n  9,735,212 bytes, SHA256 52fd8522...)\n- packaging/llvm.spec\n\nWhat it does (x86_64 only):\n- After the normal build and install, clang is relinked with\n  --emit-relocs, rewritten by BOLT with the prebuilt profile, stripped,\n  and installed in place of the ordinary clang. lld and llvm-ar are\n  not changed.\n- The build fails if the profile does not match the clang being built\n  (stale-profile ratio above 5%) or if any identity, safety or smoke\n  check fails. There is no silent fallback to the ordinary clang.\n- The profile was collected offline from 13 ARM and 10 AArch64 compile\n  workloads (generated and real LLVM sources). No training runs inside\n  the RPM build.\n- The packaged clang is about 9% larger (152.5 MB vs 139.9 MB).\n\nSpeed (historical local measurement, 30 single-file LLVM C++ -O3\ncompiles): the BOLT clang needs about 0.856x the time of the ordinary\nclang on x86_64, with similar results when compiling for ARM and\nAArch64. A QB A/B measurement of the final build is still pending.\n\nBuild cost: about 32 minutes for the BOLT stage in a local full build\n(about 19% of the total), measured on an earlier revision with the\nsame BOLT spec and helper.\n\narmv7l/aarch64: unchanged. BOLT steps and BuildRequires are guarded\nfor x86_64; the two Source lines are unconditional so the Patch lines\ngenerated by gbs stay visible on every architecture.\n\nRollback: change \"bcond_without clang_bolt\" to \"bcond_with clang_bolt\"\nfor x86_64 (one line). This disables BOLT only; Part 1 stays.\n\nValidation: PS2 was not built on its own; see the PS3 note."},{"timestamp":1794648253,"reviewer":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"message":"Patch Set 3:\n\nPatch Set 3 - adds Part 3: fixed x86_64 flags and archive checks\n\nCompare PS2 -\u003e PS3 to see Part 3 only. Files: packaging/llvm.spec,\npackaging/llvm-static-archives-native.py.\n\nWhat it does:\n- x86_64 compile and link flags are fixed to the Toolchain project\u0027s\n  effective values, so a GCC-oriented project no longer passes options\n  that clang rejects (-feliminate-unused-debug-types). Dropped and\n  unreviewed project options are printed (TIZEN_LLVM_DROPPED_FLAGS,\n  TIZEN_LLVM_FLAGS_WARNING) and do not stop the build.\n- The static-archive converter from Change 359934 gets an explicit\n  debug-info mode, a same-version check of its three tools, stricter\n  archive/ELF/relocation parsing, and signal handling.\n\nValidation of the complete series (this tree):\n- QB 1226850 (Tizen-Base-Toolchain) and 1226851 (Tizen-Base-Dev):\n  x86_64, armv7l and aarch64 builds all succeeded.\n- All 102 binary packages have the same payload as the previous QB\n  validation of these changes (1225393/1225395); 1294 static archives\n  (22,520 members) are identical member by member.\n- Local full builds of both projects match QB (Base-Dev byte-identical;\n  Toolchain debug files differ only in the Release path prefix). The\n  final clang is identical between local and QB builds, and LLDB\n  resolves 21/21 clang frames with the installed debug info.\n\nKnown open items (tracked, not blocking):\n1. QB A/B speed measurement of the final build is pending.\n2. BOLT prints 10 \"jump past end ... replacing with nop\" warnings. The\n   BOLT source treats this pattern as the result of\n   __builtin_unreachable(): a branch to the very end of a function,\n   taken only if an \"unreachable\" assumption is violated. 2 sites are\n   traced to llvm_unreachable in the source; the other 8 show the same\n   pattern; analysis continues.\n3. BOLT reports \"Failed to analyze 2804 relocations\" (relocation types\n   it does not support); a per-type census is in progress.\n4. A defensive hardening patch for the converter will follow\n   separately."}],"currentPatchSet":{"number":3,"revision":"ecb2dec72ec5afde9c6c70f166e2ac12b47c093e","parents":["13c3e223d9e1b35e4affb55255c5042f8c940f35"],"ref":"refs/changes/95/361395/3","uploader":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"createdOn":1794646378,"author":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"kind":"REWORK","sizeInsertions":2857,"sizeDeletions":67},"patchSets":[{"number":1,"revision":"c5244e13258bb541458dcd4a08254217d7c556a9","parents":["13c3e223d9e1b35e4affb55255c5042f8c940f35"],"ref":"refs/changes/95/361395/1","uploader":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"createdOn":1794500787,"author":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"kind":"REWORK","sizeInsertions":163,"sizeDeletions":3},{"number":2,"revision":"d0b2e82aa90b11251a13b67d890642bf2fa6f66c","parents":["13c3e223d9e1b35e4affb55255c5042f8c940f35"],"ref":"refs/changes/95/361395/2","uploader":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"createdOn":1794646345,"author":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"kind":"REWORK","sizeInsertions":2376,"sizeDeletions":3},{"number":3,"revision":"ecb2dec72ec5afde9c6c70f166e2ac12b47c093e","parents":["13c3e223d9e1b35e4affb55255c5042f8c940f35"],"ref":"refs/changes/95/361395/3","uploader":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"createdOn":1794646378,"author":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"kind":"REWORK","sizeInsertions":2857,"sizeDeletions":67}]}
